@host = http://localhost:5249
@adminToken = paste-token-from-login
@userToken = paste-token-of-a-regular-user
@spotId = paste-a-spot-id-from-GET-api-parking-zones
@reportId = paste-id-returned-by-POST-api-reports
@zoneId = paste-a-zone-id-from-GET-api-parking-zones
@userId = paste-a-user-id-from-GET-api-users

### Log in and copy the returned token into @adminToken; the response also has expiresAt and user (name, role)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@example.com", "password": "change-me-please" }

### Register a regular user, then log in with it and copy the token into @userToken
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Test User", "email": "user@example.com", "password": "user-pass-123" }

###
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "user@example.com", "password": "user-pass-123" }

### FR 1, FR 3: public zone listing (no login); each zone has status available, almost_full or full
GET {{host}}/api/parking/zones

### FR 2: search zones (guest). All filters optional: q (name or description), status, minAvailable, lat+lng, limit
GET {{host}}/api/parking/zones/search?q=building&status=available&minAvailable=1&lat=-7.7686&lng=110.3770

### FR 2: invalid filter returns 400 problem details
GET {{host}}/api/parking/zones/search?status=busy

### FR 4: nearest zone with free spots, measured from the zone itself (guest)
GET {{host}}/api/parking/zones/{{zoneId}}/alternate

### FR 4: same, measured from the user's position
GET {{host}}/api/parking/zones/{{zoneId}}/alternate?lat=-7.7686&lng=110.3770

### Admin: create a zone (requires the Admin role)
POST {{host}}/api/zones
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Example Zone", "totalCapacity": 10 }

### FR 5, FR 6: submit an inaccuracy report (logged-in user); 201 with status PendingReview
POST {{host}}/api/reports
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "spotId": "{{spotId}}", "description": "Spot shows free but a car is parked there." }

### FR 6: my reports and their current status
GET {{host}}/api/reports/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### One report (owner or admin; other users get 404)
GET {{host}}/api/reports/{{reportId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### FR 16: admin review queue, filter by status (PendingReview, Resolved, Dismissed)
GET {{host}}/api/reports?status=PendingReview&page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### FR 16: resolve or dismiss; a second review returns 409
POST {{host}}/api/reports/{{reportId}}/review
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "decision": "Resolved", "note": "Camera angle fixed." }

### FR 15: list users (Admin); search matches name or email, includeInactive defaults to true
GET {{host}}/api/users?search=user&page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### FR 9: the same request with a regular user's token returns 403
GET {{host}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### FR 15: one user
GET {{host}}/api/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### FR 15: edit name and role (Admin or User); demoting yourself or the last admin returns 409
PUT {{host}}/api/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Renamed User", "role": "User" }

### FR 15: deactivate; that user's login now returns 403 and their old token returns 401
POST {{host}}/api/users/{{userId}}/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### FR 15: reactivate
POST {{host}}/api/users/{{userId}}/reactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

